Subject: [PATCH 3/3] FASE 3: Advanced Audit & Rate Limiting - Security
 Monitoring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implement 2 critical security systems with 9 validation tests:

3.1 DeniedAccessLogger (120 lines)
- NestJS interceptor capturing 401/403 Unauthorized responses
- Logs to audit trail: userId, organizationId, endpoint, IP, reason
- Smart IP extraction: X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, socket.remoteAddress
- Use cases: Detect brute force, unauthorized access, compliance trails

3.2 TenantRateLimitGuard + TenantRateLimitService (290 lines)
- In-memory rate limiting (upgrade to Redis for multi-instance)
- Per-tenant limit: 1000 requests/minute per organization
- Per-user limit: 50 requests/second per user
- Returns HTTP 429 when exceeded
- Logs violations to audit trail with metadata

ObservabilityModule Integration
- Registers DeniedAccessLogger as APP_INTERCEPTOR (global)
- Registers TenantRateLimitGuard as APP_GUARD (global)
- Exports TenantRateLimitService for monitoring

Tests (9 scenarios in advanced-audit.integration.spec.ts)
✅ 401 Unauthorized logging
✅ 403 Forbidden logging
✅ IP address extraction
✅ User rate limit enforcement
✅ Tenant rate limit enforcement
✅ Audit log recording of violations
✅ Per-tenant isolation of limits
✅ Limit type differentiation (tenant vs user)
✅ Integration: denied access + rate limiting

Security Impact:
✅ Access denial visibility (compliance + incident detection)
✅ DoS protection (fair resource allocation per tenant)
✅ Anomaly detection (repeated 401s or rate limit violations)
✅ 8-layer defense with rate limiting as layer 3

